> The name comes from the legend of a devoted wife who crossed a bridge daily to deliver hot broth to her scholar husband—the warmth stayed in the broth because of the way she layered the ingredients. The secret is the order: aromatics first, then proteins, then noodles, and finally the greens. Each layer preserves the heat and creates that signature silky broth.

== Prepare the Ingredients ==

Everything is served at the table, so prep everything before you start cooking:

**Broth:**
- @chicken bones{500%g} and @chicken breast{200%g} (for the base)
- @ginger{3%slices}
- @scallions{2%stalks}
- @salt{1%tsp}

**Aromatics (raw, placed in bowl first):**
- @minced garlic{1%tsp}
- @minced ginger{1%tsp}
- @dried chili flakes{¼%tsp} (optional)
- @pickled cabbage{1%tbsp}

**Proteins (cooked briefly by the broth):**
- @sliced pork belly{150%g} (thinly sliced, raw)
- @shrimp{100%g} (peeled, raw)
- @chicken breast{100%g} (thinly sliced, raw)
- @fish ball{100%g} (optional)

**Noodles & Vegetables:**
- @rice noodles{400%g} (fresh, about 1 cm wide)
- @bean sprouts{50%g}
- @bok choy leaves{50%g}
- @chives{20%g} (cut into 5 cm pieces)

**Garnish:**
- @toasted sesame oil{1%tbsp}
- @crispy chili oil{1%tbsp}
- @coriander{10%g}
- @scallions{2%stalks} (sliced)

== Make the Broth ==

In a large pot, cover the @chicken bones{500%g} with @water{2%L}. Add @ginger{3%slices} and @scallions{2%stalks}. Bring to a boil, then reduce to a gentle simmer for ~{45%minutes}.

Strain the broth and return to the pot. Add the @chicken breast{200%g} and poach for ~{10%minutes} until cooked through. Remove and set aside. Keep the broth at a vigorous simmer—this is critical. The broth must be steaming hot (90°C+) to cook the ingredients.

Season with @salt{1%tsp}. Add more if needed.

== Assemble at the Table ==

Bring the hot broth pot to the table on a portable burner. Have all prepared ingredients arranged beautifully on a tray.

The order matters—each person assembles their own bowl:

**Layer 1 (aromatics):**
Add to a large pre-warmed bowl:
- @minced garlic{1%tsp}
- @minced ginger{1%tsp}
- @pickled cabbage{1%tbsp}
- @dried chili flakes{¼%tsp}

**Layer 2 (proteins):**
Arrange on top:
- @sliced pork belly{150%g}
- @shrimp{100%g}
- @poached chicken breast{100%g} (sliced thinly)
- @fish balls{100%g}

**Layer 3 (noodles):**
Bring the @rice noodles{400%g} directly from the pot of simmering water and pile on top. The residual heat will cook the noodles further.

**Layer 4 (vegetables):**
Add the raw vegetables on top:
- @bean sprouts{50%g}
- @bok choy{50%g}
- @chives{20%g}

**Final pour:**
Ladle the boiling broth slowly over everything—the broth should be at a rolling boil. Count to 20 as you pour, ensuring everything is submerged.

== Serve and Season ==

Wait ~{30%seconds} for the ingredients to cook in the residual heat. The pork and shrimp should turn opaque, the noodles should soften, and the broth should develop that characteristic glossy sheen.

Drizzle with:
- @toasted sesame oil{1%tbsp}
- @crispy chili oil{1%tbsp}

Garnish with @coriander{10%g} and @scallions{2%stalks}. Serve immediately with chopsticks and a spoon.

Stir the ingredients together before eating, but gently—let the broth stay clear rather than murky from over-stirring.